I want to bring this back to the recurring tunnels and subway journeys.

You described moving towards a destination, encountering interesting objects along the way, but continuing towards the goal.

I wonder whether there's a useful parallel here.

In project work, there is pressure to reach the destination:

Meet the deadline.

Resolve the technical problem.

Produce the design.

Get the migration completed.

But there are also things encountered along the way:

Different perspectives.

Alternative approaches.

People's professional investment.

Opportunities to learn.

Interesting technical possibilities.

The question isn't whether you should abandon the destination to explore every interesting object.

It's whether you can recognise which detours are valuable and which are distractions.

That's a much more nuanced challenge than simply learning to manage your ego.

